From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000013 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@local>
Date: Mon, 11 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mips: sf2000: drop stale EBase fallback vector

The ROM-path QEMU boot reached init_IRQ and then faulted while walking the
unflattened device tree. The oops state pointed at the optional
0x80002180 fallback vector area that was added for a possible stale bootloader
EBase.

That fallback writes outside Linux's normal low exception vector block, and by
this point early boot memory may already contain live OF data there. The loader
now resets CP0 EBase before jumping to Linux, and trap_init normalizes it again
before clearing BEV, so do not install the extra stale-EBase vector.
---
 arch/mips/kernel/traps.c | 8 +-------
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/mips/kernel/traps.c b/arch/mips/kernel/traps.c
index 9f8bc95886b6..742a45a85ac1 100644
--- a/arch/mips/kernel/traps.c
+++ b/arch/mips/kernel/traps.c
@@ -2470,12 +2470,8 @@
 	if (board_ebase_setup)
 		board_ebase_setup();
 
-	if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_MIPS_SF2000)) {
+	if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_MIPS_SF2000))
 		set_handler(0x180, &except_vec3_generic, 0x80);
-		/* Fallback for a stale 0x80002000 bootloader EBase. */
-		if (sf2000_rom_handoff_present())
-			set_handler(0x2180, &except_vec3_generic, 0x80);
-	}
 	sf2000_trap_tick("trap-after-pre-vector");
 
 	per_cpu_trap_init(true);
-- 
